.TH KRECT 1 "November 2026" "KRect" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
krect \- Rectangle-style window placement for KDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krect
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
KRect provides a native window-placement interface, system tray controls,
layout previews, KDE shortcut editing and placement preferences.
The placement engine runs inside KWin on Plasma 5.27 or Plasma 6.
Select a work window, then apply a layout from KRect or its tray menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start in the system tray. Show the window if a tray is unavailable.
.TP
.B \-\-language ko|en
Override the desktop language.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-smoke-test
Construct and render the interface without sending compositor commands.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH NOTES
Quitting the app leaves KWin shortcuts active. Disable KRect in the app
to stop window management. Applying preferences or reloading the engine
clears saved original placements.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/kwinrc
stores placement preferences in the Script-krect group.
.I ~/.config/autostart/org.krect.KRect.desktop
is created only when login startup is enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://github.com/ziwon/KRect
